{% extends "./layout.njk" %}
{% set section = "invite-pop" %}

{% set title = "About probation accounts" %}
{% set pageTitle = title %}

{% block content %}
  <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
      <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">{{ title }}</h1>

      <p class="govuk-body">
        'Check your probation account' is an online service where people can see information about their probation
        arrangements. It is in a pilot phase. The pilot is optional for both probation practitioners and people on
        probation. If people on probation choose not to join the pilot, it will not affect their probation arrangements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Who is eligible for the pilot</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">We are inviting people on probation who are:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>on a Community Order (CO), or on a Suspended Sentence Order (SSO)</li>
        <li>on a single order, with 1 or more requirements</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        For people who are subject to sexual offending notification requirements (MAPPA Category 1), you must check
        with the police offender manager before we can grant them access. This is to make sure their use of the account
        would not conflict with, or lead to a breach of, any civil orders they are subject to.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Who cannot take part in the pilot</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">People will not be eligible if they:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>have had their supervision suspended, for example, people in their final third or had their order terminated early</li>
        <li>are on licence, or serving concurrent orders</li>
        <li>are on the Intensive Supervision Court pilot</li>
        <li>have requirements that restrict their internet or device use</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What a probation account looks like</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">This video shows an overview of probation accounts.</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You can show or send the video to people on probation. The video will also appear the first time a person logs
        in to their account.
      </p>
      <iframe
        class="govuk-!-margin-bottom-4"
        src="https://www.veed.io/embed/00dc0b23-2d92-4136-8ab7-bebae086cc21"
        title="Walkthrough video showing an overview of probation accounts"
        width="100%"
        height="315"
        allow="fullscreen; picture-in-picture"
      ></iframe>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        <a
          class="govuk-link"
          href="https://www.veed.io/view/00dc0b23-2d92-4136-8ab7-bebae086cc21"
          rel="noreferrer noopener"
          target="_blank"
          >Open video in new tab</a
        >
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What information people on probation can and cannot see</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Probation accounts get information from multiple systems that you currently use to manage cases, for example,
        NDelius and ARNS.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">They show specific, limited information to people on probation, including:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>appointments and activities, only those facilitated by the Probation Service</li>
        <li>their requirements, including progress where applicable</li>
        <li>what is expected of them while on probation</li>
        <li>what they can expect from the Probation Service</li>
        <li>their probation officer's contact details</li>
        <li>their court order</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">It does not show:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>their case notes</li>
        <li>their CRN number</li>
        <li>any risk information, such as risk levels, scores or flags</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">What you need to do</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You need to update the systems you use to manage cases. This allows people on probation to see the latest
        information. It also means you spend less time answering queries.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You also need to check that using probation accounts will not conflict with, or lead to a breach of any of their
        order requirements, including for those subject to sexual offending notification requirements (MAPPA Category 1).
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Limitations of the pilot</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">People on probation:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>cannot change information on their account</li>
        <li>
          will need to sign in or register to
          <a
            class="govuk-link"
            href="https://www.gov.uk/using-your-gov-uk-one-login"
            rel="noreferrer noopener"
            target="_blank"
            >GOV.UK One Login</a
          >, and will need an email address for this
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        You might need to support people who struggle to access the internet or find it hard to use a device like a
        mobile phone.
      </p>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Managing access to probation accounts</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        We are sending text messages directly to people on probation to invite them to the pilot. Those who are contacted
        will need to accept the invite link within 7 days of receiving it. If the invite link expires, you can send them
        a new invite.
      </p>

      <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Invite an eligible person on probation</h3>
      <p class="govuk-body">You can also invite an eligible person on probation directly.</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Before you invite them, ask for their consent. If they consent, explain that a member of staff will call them to
        ask for feedback. The feedback call is optional and will not affect their probation.
      </p>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        <a class="govuk-button" role="button" href="/invite-pop">Invite someone</a>
      </p>

      <h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Remove access to a probation account</h3>
      <p class="govuk-body">You can remove someone's access to their online probation account at any time.</p>
      <p class="govuk-body">You might choose to do this because the person on probation:</p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>has suspended supervision, for example when starting their final third</li>
        <li>has completed their sentence</li>
        <li>has gone to prison</li>
        <li>no longer wants to access their account online</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="govuk-heading-l">Get help and support</h2>
      <p class="govuk-body">
        Email us at
        <a href="mailto:probationaccounts@justice.gov.uk" class="govuk-link">probationaccounts@justice.gov.uk</a> if:
      </p>
      <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
        <li>you have questions or feedback about the service</li>
        <li>probation accounts are not working, or something seems broken</li>
        <li>someone needs help using their probation account</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endblock %}
